title "my barista girl"
import https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Copse&display=swap
font "Copse"
bg #001236
color #fcffbd

"press space to start" l center vcenter centeralign / white monospace

music play https://opengameart.org/sites/default/files/amb_rain2_0.mp3

"It's almost closing at the coffee shop you work at, which means the few patrons you have left are the timid and quiet type." m centeralign vcenter
"All you can hear is the quiet but steady pitter-patter of the rain hitting the awning in front of the shop." m vcenter centeralign
"Suddenly, the bell above the door rings with vigor, and the rain gets louder as the door opens." m vcenter centeralign
music play https://opengameart.org/sites/default/files/under_the_rain_-_migfus20.mp3
"...a girl rushes through the door, soaking wet."
"She stops, just in front of the doorway, with her hands on her knees, trying to catch her breath." / null null true
"Finally recovering, she looks up at you, and you see her face." / null null true
"It's your crush." xl center vcenter centeralign / #f5a9b8 null true

"\"Hey there, barista girl!\" she says, smiling at you." / #f5a9b8
"Before you can even respond, she's already leaned over the counter, yapping on about how she got here." / null null true
"It's part of what you like about her. She talks more, so you don't have to." / null null true

"\"Say, I'm... actually a little cold from the rain. Don't suppose you've got anything for that?\"" / #f5a9b8
choice "You smile. \"I've got just the thing.\"" / "Make her usual coffee" coffee "Give her your jacket" jacket "Walk her home" walk / #a58dca null true

jump coffee
"\"Your usual order will warm you right up - let me make it for you!\"" / #a58dca
"\"Oh, my <i>usual</i> order?\" She lets out a little giggle. \"You know me so well.\"" / #f5a9b8 null true
"As you go to hand the coffee to her, your hands touch for a moment, startling you. You rush to pull your hand back, but knock over the coffee..." / null null true
"<mark style='color:#fcffbd;background-color:#38220f;'>...all over her shirt.</mark>" / null null true
"\"Oh my god, I'm so sorry!!\" you stammer, frantically grabbing napkins." / #a58dca null
"She just laughs, reaching across the puddle to gently grab your hand again." / null null true
"\"It's okay,\" she smiles. \"I needed to dry myself off anyways. Mind giving me a hand?\"" / #f5a9b8 null true
"\"Ah- of course!\" You rush to help her dry her shirt, her hand on top of yours." / #a58dca
"\"Er, do you want my jacket? Here, take it and warm up next to the heater.\"" / #a58dca null true
skip jacket2
end coffee

jump jacket
"\"Here, I'll give you my jacket, and you can warm up next to the heater.\"" / #a58dca
skip jacket2

jump jacket2
"Her eyes light up as she takes it. \"Are you sure? It's going to be huge on me.\"" / #f5a9b8 null true
"\"That's the point,\" you mumble, feeling your cheeks burn." / #a58dca null true
"She slips it on. The sleeves completely swallow her hands. It is the cutest thing you've ever seen."
"\"It still smells like coffee... and you,\" she whispers, hiding a very soft blush in the oversized collar." / #f5a9b8 null true
end jacket2

"You and her are the only people in the cafe left, sitting by the heater, just chatting about each others' interests for about an hour. At some point, she puts her head on your shoulder, and you don't really want to move it."
"After a while, you realize it's closing time, and leave her side to close up shop." / null null true
"\"I guess it's goodbye for today then,\" she says, in an almost disappointed tone. \"I'll just have to see you whenever I see you next.\"" / #f5a9b8 null true
choice "\"Wait, I-\"" / "Kiss her goodbye" kiss "Offer to walk her home" walk2 / #a58dca

end jacket

jump kiss
"You grab her hand before she can reach the door."
"She turns around, surprised, and before your brain can catch up with your heart, you lean in." / null null true
"And so does she." / null null true
"It's soft, warm, and tastes faintly of rain and espresso."
"When you pull back, her face is entirely red. \"...I guess then, I'll see you tomorrow, my barista girl. Good night~\"" / #f5a9b8 null true
"Before you can react, she's already out the door, into the rainy night. Still in your hoodie. You suspect you'll get it back later anyhow."
end kiss

jump walk2
"\"I can walk you home! Under my umbrella.\"" / #a58dca
skip cwalker
end walk2

jump walk
"\"My shift is over. How about I walk you home under my umbrella?\"" / #a58dca
skip cwalker
end walk

jump cwalker
"She blinks, surprised, before a bright smile takes over her face." / null null true
"\"I would love that,\" she says softly." / #f5a9b8 null true
"You lock up the shop and step out into the cold. The umbrella is just a little too small for two people."
"To stay dry, she wraps her arm around your waist and pulls you close." / null null true
"The rain is freezing, but walking next to her, you've never felt warmer." / null null true
skip home
end cwalker

jump home
"Eventually, the two of you arrive at the front steps of her apartment building."
"The porch awning shields you from the downpour, allowing you to finally close the umbrella." / null null true
"She lingers in the doorway for a moment, keys in hand, looking back up at you with a soft expression." / null null true
"\"Thank you for making sure I got back safe,\" she smiles." / #f5a9b8
"She steps inside, but before the heavy door clicks shut, she peeks her head back out." / null null true
"\"Goodnight, my barista girl.\"" / #f5a9b8 null true
"You stand there dazed for a second, and when you snap back to reality, she's already gone inside." / null null true
end home

"\"My barista girl.\" That's what she called you. ...it has a nice ring to it." m center vcenter centeralign
"You get your things in order, and head home. You can't wait to see her tomorrow."
"Fin." xl center vcenter / white